# Normalize line endings: store LF in the repository and check out LF everywhere.
#
# core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default) checked Go files out as CRLF, and every Go formatter and
# linter — gofmt, goimports, golangci-lint — then reported the whole tree as unformatted on Windows
# while CI (Linux) saw it as clean. Pinning the working tree to LF removes that difference.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts keep CRLF so cmd.exe and PowerShell can run them.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary assets must never be touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.pdf binary
